              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Hindi for a blessed offering (of food), then the Hindi for a festive dish."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: परंपरा",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "परंपरा — paramparā — \"a tradition\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "यह परंपरा सौ साल पुरानी है। yah paramparā sau sāl purānī hai. This tradition is a hundred years old."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Feminine."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "परंपरा (paramparā) is Sanskrit paramparā, \"an unbroken series, one after another\" (Monier-Williams): what passes from each generation to the next."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling what happened."
